@@ -45,6 +45,22 @@ The following options can be used to customize the CSVs returned by Datasette.
 ``?_dl=on``
     Causes Datasette to return a ``content-disposition: attachment; filename="filename.csv"`` header.
 
+``?_null=TEXT``
+    Use ``TEXT`` to represent SQL ``NULL`` values. For example,
+    ``/database/table.csv?_null=NULL`` exports those values as ``NULL``.
+    Omitting this parameter or passing ``?_null=`` keeps the default empty
+    CSV fields. Non-NULL empty strings, zero and other values are unchanged.
+
+    This works for tables, views and custom SQL queries, including every page
+    of a ``?_stream=1`` export and exports using ``?_header=off``. With
+    ``?_labels=1``, a NULL foreign key uses the marker in both its value and
+    label columns. NULL labels also use the marker, while actual empty-string
+    labels remain empty.
+
+    URL-encode the marker when constructing a URL. Unicode, commas, quotes
+    and newlines are supported and escaped using the usual CSV quoting rules.
+    The marker only affects CSV output; JSON values are unchanged.
+
